{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T11:33:06.300Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e5330e1791f32ab2f4c04d76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1678"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1678: a scoped registerRenderer replacement bypasses --output-budget and its read_output receipt reports within_budget for the native payload, not the delivered bytes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #1678 (reported 2026-11-06 against 2026.11.5 from an agent-UX review). An extension command that declares read_output participates in host output controls, but when a scoped registerRenderer (SDK) replaces the TOON rendering, the host packs and measures the native structured payload and then writes the renderer's string without applying the caller's --output-budget. In the reporter's synthetic repro, --output-budget 400 --output-row-contract emits 10,780 B (about 2,695 tokens) while read_output reports estimated_tokens 179 and within_budget true. Native JSON (1,004 B) and native TOON (716 B) controls measure correctly. With --output-budget 1 the refusal exits 2 but is itself expanded through the renderer (10,574 B). Without the receipt flag the excess remains (10,073 B). Expected: the final-output ceiling applies to the string the selected renderer returns. If it cannot fit, the host returns the bounded native refusal with a nonzero exit, never routing a refusal back through the expanding renderer. A within_budget receipt must describe the delivered bytes. Unbounded artifact rendering stays available when explicitly requested. Duplicate check: searched renderer output budget, registerRenderer output, within_budget extension; GH-560 and GH-96 (closed) cover ignored or unscoped overrides, pm-gh1552 (closed) SDK compact-versus-pretty accounting, pm-gh1662 (open) native intent budgets. This item owns post-packing custom renderer output escaping the final-byte budget. Not yet reproduced locally; the repro block in the issue is executable."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","extensions","gh:1678","output-budget","renderer","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-06T11:33:06.300Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T11:33:06.300Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The caller's --output-budget applies to the string a selected custom renderer returns, and output that cannot fit returns the bounded native output_budget_exceeded refusal with exit 2; A refusal is never routed back through an expanding custom renderer; read_output estimated_tokens and within_budget describe the delivered bytes of a custom rendering; Explicitly unbounded custom rendering stays available; A spec with a synthetic extension renderer asserts the bounded and unbounded behaviour in TOON and JSON, and a negative control that measures the native payload instead fails it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1552","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-06T11:33:06.300Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1662","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-06T11:33:06.300Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"d1ed28ae3111d912837276514547e229e0083478743145fbfc8b446259712cec","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"def4ecde1583a45d00f57af1ffa332414c8e6a60c27612be59ed896fb33ace3e"}
